        <mxCell id="devhost-73" parent="devhostV4" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontColor=#555555;fontStyle=2;" value="&lt;b&gt;V4&lt;/b&gt; · Each other developer gets their own Linux account, home, clone and branch, and their own copy of the app (its own Compose project and ports, mapped back to localhost on their PC). An admin adds a developer with one command: the account, their SSH keys from GitHub, and their IP on the firewall list. SSH stays limited to listed IPs. Stacks fit in memory because the UI is served built, as in V2. Anyone with Docker access has admin-level control of the VM, so it suits developers who trust each other." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="1740" x="40" y="1120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
